1
00:00:06,156 --> 00:00:09,793
Heiwa Fansubs Presents:
"Great Detective Conan"
Challenge to Kudo Shin'ichi

2
00:00:14,431 --> 00:00:17,267
Oh! It's that case!

3
00:00:20,170 --> 00:00:22,939
That wedding-party case
I settled at a crack!

4
00:00:23,407 --> 00:00:26,777
Ah, the one where it was
your fault someone died.

5
00:00:27,377 --> 00:00:30,047
The case of the party where
you got overly excited...

6
00:00:30,147 --> 00:00:31,948
...and, thanks to that,
gave an opening for someone to be killed.

7
00:00:32,049 --> 00:00:33,417
You're giving me a bad reputation!

8
00:00:33,517 --> 00:00:35,018
That was the case where...

9
00:00:35,118 --> 00:00:38,255
...after you had forced the bride and groom
to kiss one another, someone died, isn't it?

10
00:00:38,355 --> 00:00:39,790
Foolishness!

11
00:00:40,057 --> 00:00:46,229
Ran, I was trying to protect your
precious boy here's First Kiss.

12
00:00:48,031 --> 00:00:49,733
Kiss?

13
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:51,168
He's wrong, wrong, wrong.

14
00:00:51,268 --> 00:00:53,703
Hmm... What's this about?

15
00:00:53,804 --> 00:00:55,205
Wait and I'll tell you!

16
00:00:55,305 --> 00:00:56,840
How do I put this...

17
00:00:56,940 --> 00:00:58,775
It was your fault it happened.

18
00:00:58,875 --> 00:01:00,377
Eh?

19
00:01:01,378 --> 00:01:03,246
"Kensuke - Kanon
Congratulations on Your Marriage"

20
00:01:03,680 --> 00:01:05,115
Are you serious?

21
00:01:05,849 --> 00:01:07,350
Yes.

22
00:01:07,818 --> 00:01:09,619
What'll we do?

23
00:01:09,953 --> 00:01:12,155
"What'll we do," you ask...

24
00:01:12,556 --> 00:01:14,191
I'm getting married today.

25
00:01:14,291 --> 00:01:17,027
I won't let you off easy.
I've got my pride.

26
00:01:17,027 --> 00:01:18,295
"Bridegroom, 'Diavel's Kiss' Manager
Motoki Kensuke"

27
00:01:18,395 --> 00:01:19,463
Even if you say that...

28
00:01:19,563 --> 00:01:23,400
I'll be expecting a more solid answer.
By the end of the day.

29
00:01:26,002 --> 00:01:29,806
"Bride
Shimabara Kanon"

30
00:01:32,676 --> 00:01:35,579
Whaa! So beautiful!

31
00:01:36,113 --> 00:01:37,848
Congratulations on your wedding.

32
00:01:38,615 --> 00:01:40,083
Thank you.

33
00:01:40,884 --> 00:01:42,319
Nana...

34
00:01:42,419 --> 00:01:44,020
Is something happening between
you and Kei-chan?

35
00:01:44,121 --> 00:01:45,388
Stop it.

36
00:01:45,489 --> 00:01:48,458
There's no way anything could happen between
your best friend and the one you're marrying.

37
00:01:48,558 --> 00:01:51,661
You and I are friends.
Motoki-san's a friend, too.

38
00:01:51,761 --> 00:01:53,296
That's all.

39
00:01:53,396 --> 00:01:54,698
I see...

40
00:01:54,798 --> 00:01:56,800
- Sorry if I said anything weird.
- No.

41
00:01:56,933 --> 00:01:59,369
- Then, see you later.
- Later.

42
00:01:59,769 --> 00:02:01,872
Ah, but Kanon.

43
00:02:01,905 --> 00:02:03,039
"Friend of the Bride
Masumoto Nana"

44
00:02:03,140 --> 00:02:07,978
I won't be me, but if something does happen,
it won't be my responsibility.

45
00:02:08,612 --> 00:02:10,080
Eh?

46
00:02:11,581 --> 00:02:15,051
If such a thing happened,
I might have to kill you two.

47
00:02:16,286 --> 00:02:18,288
Whaa... scary.

48
00:02:25,462 --> 00:02:27,364
Penalty game?
What's that?

49
00:02:27,664 --> 00:02:30,000
You had a brain lock
at lunch, didn't you?

50
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:32,335
You said you'd play a penalty game
if you lost, didn't you?

51
00:02:32,435 --> 00:02:35,238
- Kudo-kun, you lost, didn't you?
- You lost, you lost!

52
00:02:35,338 --> 00:02:37,107
You guys won by cheating.

53
00:02:37,207 --> 00:02:38,875
It wasn't cheating.
It was strategy.

54
00:02:38,975 --> 00:02:40,510
- Right?
- Right?

55
00:02:40,610 --> 00:02:42,145
Nothing I can do.

56
00:02:42,245 --> 00:02:43,413
And?

57
00:02:43,513 --> 00:02:49,486
Shin'ichi can't turn down any favors
from anyone for the entire day.

58
00:02:50,387 --> 00:02:51,488
"Shin'ichi's Childhood Friend
Mori Ran"

59
00:02:51,588 --> 00:02:54,457
Since this is a penalty game,
make sure you do it right.

60
00:02:55,325 --> 00:02:57,027
- Here, take this.
- Yes, yes, I've got it.

61
00:02:57,127 --> 00:03:00,230
"Shin'ichi and Ran's Fellow Student
Suzuki Sonoko"

62
00:03:01,531 --> 00:03:06,436
Then from here you can treat me
at a family restaurant...

63
00:03:07,771 --> 00:03:08,939
Yes?

64
00:03:09,306 --> 00:03:10,740
Sir?

65
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:12,876
Eh? You need a favor?

66
00:03:19,783 --> 00:03:22,652
Kyaa! He's really come!

67
00:03:24,020 --> 00:03:25,622
It's the real Shin'ichi-kun!

68
00:03:25,722 --> 00:03:26,957
"Friend of Bride: Niizuma Ayaka
Friend of the Bride: Onna Yuka"

69
00:03:27,057 --> 00:03:29,159
"Why are these girls
dressed up so flashily for?"

70
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:31,928
"Private Detective
Mori Kogoro"

71
00:03:32,028 --> 00:03:33,363
Girls...

72
00:03:33,463 --> 00:03:37,434
Don't forget the one who called for this foremost
high school detective, Kudo Shin'ichi-kun...

73
00:03:37,534 --> 00:03:42,205
...was I, the super-great detective,
Mori Kogoro!

74
00:03:43,206 --> 00:03:45,875
Sir, what's this
"deep-cover investigation" about?

75
00:03:46,076 --> 00:03:47,344
A wedding.

76
00:03:47,444 --> 00:03:48,745
Huh?!

77
00:03:49,212 --> 00:03:52,315
All of these kittens are regular customers
here at "Diavel's Kiss."

78
00:03:52,415 --> 00:03:56,386
And the Master of the place and his
regular customer Kanon-chan are getting married.

79
00:03:56,586 --> 00:04:00,156
So they asked me to arrange
and hold this party for them.

80
00:04:00,290 --> 00:04:03,760
Take care of these right away.
As a favor.

81
00:04:03,860 --> 00:04:06,596
Eh?! Another favor...

82
00:04:08,865 --> 00:04:10,667
That Nana...

83
00:04:11,067 --> 00:04:13,303
"What'll we do," she asks.

84
00:04:15,972 --> 00:04:19,576
I'm hungry.
Ken-chan, don't you have anything?

85
00:04:19,876 --> 00:04:22,512
We're having the party right now.
You want to eat before that?

86
00:04:22,646 --> 00:04:26,216
But I can't just stuff my face
in front of everyone wearing this, can I?

87
00:04:26,383 --> 00:04:29,085
I'll have to starve until I'm a bride.

88
00:04:29,185 --> 00:04:31,855
Ah, this'll do fine.

89
00:04:31,955 --> 00:04:33,623
That's yesterday's leftovers.

90
00:04:33,723 --> 00:04:35,392
It's okay, it's okay.

91
00:04:36,226 --> 00:04:39,095
Oi, that's my secret ingredient;
if you put that in, it'll taste bad.

92
00:04:39,296 --> 00:04:40,897
I know...

93
00:04:43,266 --> 00:04:45,635
Ken-chan's "Final Curry" is delicious.

94
00:04:51,107 --> 00:04:52,509
Excuse me.

95
00:04:52,742 --> 00:04:55,645
Yes, I'm in your debt.
Yeah, yes.

96
00:04:57,247 --> 00:04:58,715
Excuse me.

97
00:04:59,215 --> 00:05:00,717
Excuse me.

98
00:05:01,551 --> 00:05:05,755
It really is Kudo-kun.
Incredible!

99
00:05:07,123 --> 00:05:09,292
Could I ask you to sign this?

100
00:05:09,592 --> 00:05:12,896
Ah, thanks for your hard work.

101
00:05:14,764 --> 00:05:18,468
Ah, that's right, Kudo-kun.
Could I ask a favor of you?

102
00:05:19,235 --> 00:05:22,605
Ah, heavy!
I'm being run around like a slave.

103
00:05:22,972 --> 00:05:25,342
I can't. I just can't.

104
00:05:25,842 --> 00:05:27,510
You just can't?

105
00:05:28,078 --> 00:05:29,946
Then, I guess I'll have to give birth.

106
00:05:30,046 --> 00:05:31,147
Eh?

107
00:05:31,381 --> 00:05:33,650
Because I don't want to
cause you trouble, Motoki-kun.

108
00:05:34,050 --> 00:05:38,722
Seems heavy for them, too.
Think I'll take a detour.

109
00:05:48,064 --> 00:05:49,866
Ken-chan, something happen?

110
00:05:49,966 --> 00:05:53,002
Eh? Ah, it was nothing.
Just work.

111
00:05:54,304 --> 00:05:58,875
Ken-chan, truth is,
I need to say I'm sorry to you.

112
00:05:58,975 --> 00:06:00,143
Eh?

113
00:06:00,377 --> 00:06:04,447
I've been suspicious of you and Nana lately.

114
00:06:05,014 --> 00:06:06,750
The two of you have
been meeting, haven't you?

115
00:06:07,150 --> 00:06:08,585
Ah...

116
00:06:09,219 --> 00:06:10,687
Look, it was about that.

117
00:06:10,787 --> 00:06:14,457
Nana-chan's business.
She's looking to buy health foods.

118
00:06:14,557 --> 00:06:17,260
That's it!
She's decided to do that, has she?

119
00:06:17,527 --> 00:06:20,430
Yet I thought something was going on.

120
00:06:21,264 --> 00:06:22,532
I'm sorry.

121
00:06:22,632 --> 00:06:23,833
Not at all.

122
00:06:24,868 --> 00:06:27,036
- Sorry.
- It's okay.

123
00:06:35,879 --> 00:06:38,815
Could it be you were about to kiss just now...

124
00:06:39,048 --> 00:06:40,784
Ah, I caught you right in the middle of it.

125
00:06:40,817 --> 00:06:41,785
No...

126
00:06:41,885 --> 00:06:46,923
I had no intention of bothering you,
but I ended up doing something boorish.

127
00:06:48,091 --> 00:06:51,060
Ah! Ah! Curry! Curry!

128
00:06:51,161 --> 00:06:52,228
What'll we do?

129
00:06:53,296 --> 00:06:55,532
Thanks for waiting!

130
00:06:55,632 --> 00:06:59,169
The entrance of the Bride and Groom!

131
00:06:59,436 --> 00:07:01,104
Cue! Cue!

132
00:07:04,340 --> 00:07:05,508
Congratulations!

133
00:07:07,076 --> 00:07:08,378
Thank you!

134
00:07:11,948 --> 00:07:14,451
Set the night on fire!
Brush your teeth!

135
00:07:15,251 --> 00:07:17,921
Sir, what's with this stain?

136
00:07:18,021 --> 00:07:19,722
I got some curry on it.

137
00:07:19,823 --> 00:07:21,257
You some school kid?

138
00:07:21,925 --> 00:07:23,860
Excuse me. Telegram.

139
00:07:23,960 --> 00:07:25,862
Thanks.

140
00:07:25,962 --> 00:07:27,464
Big round of applause.
Please give them a big round of applause!

141
00:07:28,565 --> 00:07:29,732
"If you have an affair, I'll kill you"

142
00:07:29,833 --> 00:07:30,500
"I'll kill you"

143
00:07:33,036 --> 00:07:35,371
A photo, a photo.
Look this way, look this way.

144
00:07:35,472 --> 00:07:38,308
To your left, your left!
Say cheese!

145
00:07:40,677 --> 00:07:44,180
Ehh... well then, on the occasion of
Motoki Kensuke-san...

146
00:07:44,280 --> 00:07:47,817
...and the soon to be Motoki Kanon-san...

147
00:07:47,917 --> 00:07:52,555
...but currently Shimabara Kanon-san's wedding.

148
00:07:53,022 --> 00:07:54,524
Kanpai!

149
00:07:54,958 --> 00:07:57,060
- Kanpai!
- Kanpai!

150
00:08:01,197 --> 00:08:03,666
You could say the start
of these two being together...

151
00:08:03,766 --> 00:08:07,504
...came after Kanon-san had eaten
the "Final Curry"...

152
00:08:07,604 --> 00:08:11,541
...that the bridegroom had made for her
and she became addicted to it.

153
00:08:11,641 --> 00:08:15,178
Well, long ago when
Tokugawa Ieyasu was alive...

154
00:08:15,278 --> 00:08:19,349
Sir!
People hate long speeches.

155
00:08:23,152 --> 00:08:26,356
Eh... Well then, it's presumptuous of me...

156
00:08:26,656 --> 00:08:32,896
...but I, Mori Kogoro, will now read out
the congratulatory telegrams.

157
00:08:36,199 --> 00:08:38,301
"Congratulations on your marriage!"

158
00:08:38,401 --> 00:08:42,272
"Be happy for eternity!
From Michiko."

159
00:08:42,839 --> 00:08:46,276
That's pretty ordinary, isn't it?
It's ordinary, I'd say.

160
00:08:48,044 --> 00:08:49,779
This one doesn't have a sender!

161
00:08:52,115 --> 00:08:53,816
This one'll be a big hit!

162
00:08:54,784 --> 00:08:57,921
"If you have an affair, I'll kill you!"

163
00:08:59,122 --> 00:09:01,891
Ah, ala?
Something wrong?

164
00:09:02,625 --> 00:09:04,427
Eh? What's that?

165
00:09:04,527 --> 00:09:06,763
That's a seriously
super-popular thing to do.

166
00:09:11,301 --> 00:09:13,403
Well then, um...
so much for the telegrams.

167
00:09:13,603 --> 00:09:16,639
So that there are no worries at all
about these two cheating on one another...

168
00:09:16,806 --> 00:09:18,875
...let's have them kiss!

169
00:09:18,975 --> 00:09:21,311
Eh?
Well, don't ask us for that!

170
00:09:21,411 --> 00:09:23,146
That's embarrassing!

171
00:09:23,246 --> 00:09:25,148
A kiss is an indispensible part of a wedding!

172
00:09:25,214 --> 00:09:26,849
Kiss, kiss, kiss...

173
00:09:26,950 --> 00:09:28,785
Don't let it die down!
Make 'em do it!

174
00:09:28,885 --> 00:09:31,888
Kiss! Kiss!

175
00:09:32,088 --> 00:09:35,925
Kiss! Kiss! Kiss! Kiss!

176
00:09:42,832 --> 00:09:45,935
I'm vexed at their happiness!
Let's really get drunk today!

177
00:09:46,035 --> 00:09:47,136
Right!

178
00:09:49,072 --> 00:09:53,376
Okay! All of today's dishes were homemade
by the bridegroom himself!

179
00:09:53,476 --> 00:09:55,612
Yeah!

180
00:09:56,079 --> 00:09:57,747
"If you have an affair, I'll kill you"

181
00:09:57,847 --> 00:10:00,216
He also personally shook the shaker
and made all the cocktails!

182
00:10:01,317 --> 00:10:05,421
"Let's hope this telegram
is nothing but a prank."

183
00:10:08,858 --> 00:10:11,928
Say, Shin'ichi-kun.
Touch my cheeks.

184
00:10:11,995 --> 00:10:12,862
Eh?!

185
00:10:12,962 --> 00:10:14,564
Will you touch my cheeks?

186
00:10:14,664 --> 00:10:17,400
If not my cheeks,
then will you touch some other place?

187
00:10:17,667 --> 00:10:19,135
Say, say, touch me.

188
00:10:19,235 --> 00:10:20,703
Ah! Miss, are you okay?

189
00:10:20,803 --> 00:10:22,872
Ah!
You're staring at her breasts!

190
00:10:22,972 --> 00:10:24,007
I'm not!

191
00:10:24,107 --> 00:10:25,875
What? What, what!?

192
00:10:26,209 --> 00:10:27,710
Hey, boy detective!

193
00:10:28,044 --> 00:10:30,013
It's still way too early for you
to be investigating that!

194
00:10:30,446 --> 00:10:31,914
I'll take over from here.

195
00:10:32,248 --> 00:10:35,918
Kogoro-chan, rather than that,
go talk to Nana.

196
00:10:36,519 --> 00:10:40,123
Abandoning this drunk young lady
would be irresponsible of me, now wouldn't it?

197
00:10:40,890 --> 00:10:43,026
I'll sober you up.
Now, now.

198
00:10:43,459 --> 00:10:46,396
Are you okay!?
Are you okay, Yuka-chan?!

199
00:10:46,496 --> 00:10:47,730
Hey!

200
00:10:47,830 --> 00:10:49,732
Kogoro!

201
00:10:49,899 --> 00:10:52,101
Are you jumping ship for Yuka?

202
00:10:52,268 --> 00:10:53,703
Nana-chaaan!

203
00:10:54,404 --> 00:10:56,606
You're the most beautiful one in the world!

204
00:10:57,874 --> 00:11:00,977
Then, buy me some
alligator juice this time.

205
00:11:01,344 --> 00:11:04,213
Let's have some alligator juice with gusto!
(Gusto = Mori Mori)

206
00:11:05,715 --> 00:11:08,484
The bridegroom's very popular, isn't he?

207
00:11:08,851 --> 00:11:10,353
That's true.

208
00:11:10,453 --> 00:11:13,923
Because he's so handsome, isn't he?
Even I wanted to date him...

209
00:11:14,023 --> 00:11:17,160
"Looks like that telegram
was nothing more than a prank."

210
00:11:17,293 --> 00:11:19,729
I should have just pushed myself onto him.

211
00:11:21,097 --> 00:11:23,933
Ayaka.
You shouldn't be saying such things.

212
00:11:24,033 --> 00:11:25,501
Eh... Is that right?

213
00:11:25,601 --> 00:11:27,270
Of course that's right, isn't it?

214
00:11:27,370 --> 00:11:29,706
Ala? It's rare to see you two fighting.
Something happen?

215
00:11:32,008 --> 00:11:33,776
- Nothing at all!
- Nothing at all!

216
00:11:33,976 --> 00:11:34,944
Really?

217
00:11:35,044 --> 00:11:36,412
- Right?
- Right?

218
00:11:38,448 --> 00:11:40,917
More importantly, look,
the bride should drink up, too.

219
00:11:42,151 --> 00:11:45,321
Bridegroom!
Make a cocktail for your bride.

220
00:11:45,588 --> 00:11:48,124
Ah... yeah.
I'll make one.

221
00:11:51,761 --> 00:11:55,098
Ah, you mustn't! Shin'ichi-kun,
don't look away and just look at me!

222
00:11:55,198 --> 00:11:58,468
Ayaka, no!
Shin'ichi-kun's mine!

223
00:11:58,568 --> 00:12:01,537
Shin'ichi-kun, you can't have her!
Nana-chan's Kogoro-chan's!

224
00:12:03,773 --> 00:12:05,908
Say, Shin'ichi-kun, can I have this?

225
00:12:06,008 --> 00:12:06,843
Eh?!

226
00:12:06,943 --> 00:12:09,378
Nana! If you want a juice,
I'll bring you a new one.

227
00:12:09,479 --> 00:12:11,714
No! I want Shin'ichi-kun's!

228
00:12:11,814 --> 00:12:14,283
It came out! Nana's "I want."

229
00:12:14,684 --> 00:12:16,052
"I want"?

230
00:12:16,152 --> 00:12:19,756
Look, from long ago, Nana's had a
reckless want for what other people have.

231
00:12:19,856 --> 00:12:24,193
Food, drinks, toys, men,
she wants whatever anyone else has.

232
00:12:24,293 --> 00:12:26,462
No, not men.

233
00:12:26,562 --> 00:12:29,632
But, the grass on the other side
is always greener, right?

234
00:12:29,665 --> 00:12:32,869
That's why it's...
just a bad habit of mine.

235
00:12:33,736 --> 00:12:35,004
Nana!

236
00:12:35,371 --> 00:12:37,440
My grass is even greener!

237
00:12:37,540 --> 00:12:40,409
Shake it up, baby now! Wow!

238
00:12:46,916 --> 00:12:48,551
Thanks for waiting.

239
00:12:49,051 --> 00:12:52,388
The special cocktail, "Kanon."
My original creation.

240
00:12:52,855 --> 00:12:54,323
Thank you.

241
00:12:54,423 --> 00:12:56,459
- Then, make one for me, too.
- Eh?

242
00:12:56,559 --> 00:12:58,361
A cocktail you'll call "Nana."

243
00:12:58,461 --> 00:13:00,296
Ah, here!
Make me an "Ayaka-rin"!

244
00:13:00,396 --> 00:13:02,031
I'll take a "Great Detective"!

245
00:13:02,131 --> 00:13:04,500
Ah, very well.
I'll go make them right now.

246
00:13:06,169 --> 00:13:10,373
Then, I'm off to the restroom.

247
00:13:19,682 --> 00:13:21,117
Here, your "Ayaka-rin."

248
00:13:21,450 --> 00:13:22,919
Whaa, thank you!

249
00:13:23,019 --> 00:13:24,153
Your "Great Detective."

250
00:13:24,253 --> 00:13:27,523
Oh! You've magnificently expressed
the feelings of transparency that I hold.

251
00:13:31,194 --> 00:13:32,461
Hmm...

252
00:13:32,562 --> 00:13:35,398
Motoki-kun, so this is how you think of me.

253
00:13:35,498 --> 00:13:36,532
Eh?

254
00:13:37,166 --> 00:13:39,435
Tequila, gin and red wine.

255
00:13:39,869 --> 00:13:41,537
I'm a monster!

256
00:13:41,637 --> 00:13:43,606
I want to drink more of something else!

257
00:13:44,740 --> 00:13:46,209
You can drink this.

258
00:13:46,309 --> 00:13:48,678
It seems I'm a little drunk anyhow.

259
00:13:48,911 --> 00:13:50,646
I'm going to the restroom.

260
00:13:56,552 --> 00:13:59,655
This "Kanon" looks too sweet...

261
00:14:00,990 --> 00:14:02,124
I want this!

262
00:14:03,993 --> 00:14:05,661
Nana, you're terrible!

263
00:14:07,763 --> 00:14:08,865
Yeah...

264
00:14:09,165 --> 00:14:11,901
Vodka in a melon liqueur, huh?

265
00:14:21,544 --> 00:14:23,145
Nana-san! Nana-san!

266
00:14:23,246 --> 00:14:24,547
- Nana-chan!
- Nana-chan!

267
00:14:24,647 --> 00:14:26,082
- Nana-san!
- Nana-chan!

268
00:14:26,816 --> 00:14:28,284
Nana?!

269
00:14:29,785 --> 00:14:31,520
She's dead...

270
00:14:34,891 --> 00:14:39,095
This is... poisoning?!

271
00:14:43,466 --> 00:14:45,301
The criminal is you!

272
00:14:46,302 --> 00:14:48,671
You put poison in that cocktail, didn't you!

273
00:14:48,771 --> 00:14:49,772
Eh!?

274
00:14:49,872 --> 00:14:53,309
I'll bet my life as a detective by
declaring that you are the criminal!

275
00:14:53,409 --> 00:14:55,845
Why? Why is it me!?

276
00:14:55,945 --> 00:14:57,413
Stop your struggling!

277
00:14:57,513 --> 00:15:00,416
Even if you are called a handsome rascal,
it's not wrong to give yourself up!

278
00:15:00,516 --> 00:15:01,817
I'm telling you, I didn't do it!

279
00:15:01,918 --> 00:15:05,121
It's true Motoki-san had the opportunity
to put poison into the cocktails."

280
00:15:05,221 --> 00:15:07,890
"There seems to have been some complicated
circumstances between him and Nana-san."

281
00:15:07,990 --> 00:15:11,127
"The sort of circumstances that makes him
likeliest to being the criminal."

282
00:15:11,227 --> 00:15:12,428
That's right...

283
00:15:12,528 --> 00:15:13,729
"MPD Investigation Unit One
Sato Miwako"

284
00:15:13,829 --> 00:15:15,031
Eh?!

285
00:15:15,131 --> 00:15:18,234
There were no poisons
detected in the drink?

286
00:15:19,802 --> 00:15:23,639
The cause of death was due to
an allergic reaction? A shock death...

287
00:15:25,174 --> 00:15:27,243
An allergy to soba...
(Buckwheat flour used in noodles)

288
00:15:27,843 --> 00:15:29,445
Roger.

289
00:15:29,545 --> 00:15:31,480
The cause of death
was an allergic reaction to soba?

290
00:15:31,580 --> 00:15:32,915
Yes.

291
00:15:33,449 --> 00:15:37,753
Without realizing it,
Nana-san had ingested some soba.

292
00:15:37,954 --> 00:15:41,757
But there wasn't any soba
in any of the dishes.

293
00:15:42,024 --> 00:15:43,926
Of course there wouldn't be!

294
00:15:44,060 --> 00:15:46,495
I knew about Nana's allergy.

295
00:15:47,129 --> 00:15:49,465
The thing is, this is an Italian restaurant.

296
00:15:50,066 --> 00:15:52,168
There's no reason for me
to even have soba around!

297
00:15:52,268 --> 00:15:54,670
Did anyone else know about her allergy?

298
00:15:54,770 --> 00:15:56,973
I think we all knew about it.

299
00:16:00,176 --> 00:16:02,945
Well, I guess after thinking about it,
you are the criminal!

300
00:16:03,045 --> 00:16:04,847
Confess you handsome rascal!

301
00:16:04,947 --> 00:16:06,716
I didn't do it, I tell you!

302
00:16:07,383 --> 00:16:09,852
That's right.
You're a great detective, right?

303
00:16:09,952 --> 00:16:12,722
As a favor! Please!
Prove my innocence!

304
00:16:12,822 --> 00:16:14,423
Eh? A favor?

305
00:16:14,523 --> 00:16:16,359
"Oh no! Another favor."

306
00:16:16,459 --> 00:16:17,927
Shin'ichi-kun!

307
00:16:21,197 --> 00:16:23,966
Look, that's annoying.

308
00:16:24,066 --> 00:16:26,268
All you've been doing
is sighing since earlier.

309
00:16:26,369 --> 00:16:28,070
Ah... sorry.

310
00:16:30,473 --> 00:16:32,341
Rather than a penalty game...

311
00:16:32,441 --> 00:16:35,511
...you should've just asked him nicely
to treat you dinner, shouldn't you?

312
00:16:35,911 --> 00:16:37,813
That's too embarrassing!

313
00:16:40,683 --> 00:16:42,518
Suit yourself.

314
00:16:42,852 --> 00:16:44,053
"MPD Investigation Unit One
Tagaki Wataru"

315
00:16:44,153 --> 00:16:46,956
It's impossible for me to have soba here.
That's just stupid!

316
00:16:47,056 --> 00:16:50,393
Unless we can prove
there's no soba in this store...

317
00:16:50,493 --> 00:16:53,295
...then we can't prove your innocence.

318
00:16:53,396 --> 00:16:55,197
That Ran did something unnecessary.

319
00:16:56,932 --> 00:16:58,601
What is it?
Are you okay, Tagaki-kun?

320
00:16:58,701 --> 00:17:00,936
Somehow, this is pepper...

321
00:17:01,437 --> 00:17:02,972
May I try it?

322
00:17:07,676 --> 00:17:09,412
Oi, oi, will you be okay?

323
00:17:10,946 --> 00:17:13,382
This is Sansho, isn't it?
(a Japanese pepper)

324
00:17:13,482 --> 00:17:15,384
What dishes do you use Sansho for?

325
00:17:15,484 --> 00:17:18,020
Eh? That's...

326
00:17:19,755 --> 00:17:23,426
Oi! What is it?
Not going to answer?

327
00:17:23,526 --> 00:17:27,596
I use it as the secret ingredient in my
"Final Curry" that I serve here.

328
00:17:28,230 --> 00:17:29,532
Curry?

329
00:17:29,632 --> 00:17:32,301
"Excuse me. Excuse me."

330
00:17:53,622 --> 00:17:55,024
It's soba.

331
00:17:56,559 --> 00:17:58,527
I guess you were the criminal after all!

332
00:17:58,727 --> 00:18:02,131
I know! You and Nana-chan
were having an affair, weren't you?

333
00:18:02,331 --> 00:18:06,368
Then, using a trick of some kind,
you made Nana-chan ingest soba, didn't you?

334
00:18:06,602 --> 00:18:09,772
That's stupid!
Why was soba in there?!

335
00:18:09,872 --> 00:18:12,441
Motoki-san, could you
come with us to our office?

336
00:18:12,741 --> 00:18:15,311
I honestly didn't kill anyone.

337
00:18:15,411 --> 00:18:19,281
Ken-chan, you really weren't having an affair?

338
00:18:19,381 --> 00:18:22,985
"Assuming she's the one
who added in the soba..."

339
00:18:23,285 --> 00:18:28,491
"...the problem is how did she then
get it into Nana-san's mouth?"

340
00:18:30,993 --> 00:18:35,097
Ala? The police?

341
00:18:35,564 --> 00:18:40,302
I know!
This is the great detective's game, isn't it?

342
00:18:40,402 --> 00:18:44,440
Oi, oi Miss!
You're not only drunk, but half-asleep.

343
00:18:44,707 --> 00:18:46,475
Ah, then!

344
00:18:46,642 --> 00:18:49,678
Let's change it to the King game!
(a drinking-dare game)

345
00:18:50,346 --> 00:18:54,650
The King'll be... me!

346
00:18:57,253 --> 00:18:58,721
Shin'ichi-kun.

347
00:18:59,088 --> 00:19:01,190
The King says kiss me!

348
00:19:02,158 --> 00:19:03,659
Please, kiss me.

349
00:19:03,759 --> 00:19:05,694
"This is bad! Another favor!"

350
00:19:12,568 --> 00:19:14,270
"I just can't do it!"

351
00:19:18,140 --> 00:19:19,808
You mustn't, Yuka-chan.

352
00:19:20,476 --> 00:19:24,246
How many have fallen into the bottomless
Dante's Inferno of my pheromones?

353
00:19:26,048 --> 00:19:29,451
Nana-chan's the one essential for my heart.

354
00:19:33,389 --> 00:19:35,257
I see!

355
00:19:35,925 --> 00:19:37,726
So that's how it is!

356
00:19:38,827 --> 00:19:42,131
No, no...
There's nothing between Yuka-chan and me.

357
00:19:42,231 --> 00:19:44,600
No, I don't have enough yet.

358
00:19:44,967 --> 00:19:47,203
There's still something
I should get for proof.

359
00:19:47,303 --> 00:19:48,737
Proof?

360
00:19:49,171 --> 00:19:50,973
I've seen it.

361
00:19:51,140 --> 00:19:55,077
The one and only truth behind this incident.

362
00:19:55,177 --> 00:19:56,278
Eh?

363
00:19:56,378 --> 00:19:58,113
Shin'ichi-kun...

364
00:19:58,847 --> 00:20:01,016
You can prove my innocence?

365
00:20:01,116 --> 00:20:03,152
The one who killed Nana-chan was...

366
00:20:05,254 --> 00:20:07,156
The one who killed Nana-chan was...

367
00:20:09,391 --> 00:20:11,393
The one who killed Nana-chan was...

368
00:20:11,493 --> 00:20:12,695
Yeah!

369
00:20:13,362 --> 00:20:14,997
I guess it was Motoki-san.

370
00:20:15,097 --> 00:20:17,066
- Eh?
- Ah, the pepper guy.

371
00:20:17,166 --> 00:20:18,934
However...

372
00:20:19,034 --> 00:20:21,103
...he didn't kill her alone.

373
00:20:21,937 --> 00:20:23,639
To be accurate about it...

374
00:20:23,739 --> 00:20:30,379
...Motoki-san committed an act of murder
without knowing that he was killing.

375
00:20:30,579 --> 00:20:33,716
Kudo-kun, have you found
some new evidence?

376
00:20:34,416 --> 00:20:35,684
This.

377
00:20:37,453 --> 00:20:40,856
When you run an investigative analysis
on this stain, then probably soba...

378
00:20:41,190 --> 00:20:43,525
...an ingredient of soba will show up.

379
00:20:43,626 --> 00:20:46,161
But that has nothing to do with Nana-chan.

380
00:20:46,262 --> 00:20:47,963
But it does.

381
00:20:48,230 --> 00:20:52,034
It was yours and Kanon-san's fidelity kiss.

382
00:20:53,035 --> 00:20:54,503
I don't get it!

383
00:20:54,970 --> 00:20:58,741
How is this man and Kanon-san's kiss
connected to a murder?

384
00:20:58,874 --> 00:21:03,312
Motoki-san, you're concealing it, aren't you?

385
00:21:04,246 --> 00:21:06,015
Well, what you're concealing is...

386
00:21:06,448 --> 00:21:09,618
I don't know what the emotions are behind it.

387
00:21:09,885 --> 00:21:14,890
So then, I'll prove the truth piece by piece.

388
00:21:15,758 --> 00:21:21,864
First, there wasn't any soba in the cocktails
that Nana-chan and Ayaka-san drank.

389
00:21:22,064 --> 00:21:28,771
That is, Nana-san had ingested soba
even before she drank Ayaka-san's cocktail.

390
00:21:28,971 --> 00:21:30,406
In other words...

391
00:21:30,606 --> 00:21:33,709
...we can infer it happened between
when she said she was going to the restroom...

392
00:21:33,842 --> 00:21:35,577
...and when she came back out
down the hallway.

393
00:21:35,911 --> 00:21:37,780
That coincides exactly with the time...

394
00:21:38,981 --> 00:21:45,120
...when Motoki-san said he would make
the cocktails and stepped out.

395
00:21:46,221 --> 00:21:51,860
I recall that Nana-san went out
just after Motoki-san had left.

396
00:21:51,960 --> 00:21:55,698
"Then, I'm off to the restroom."

397
00:21:56,865 --> 00:22:01,270
That means that was the chance
to give Nana-san some soba to eat.

398
00:22:01,537 --> 00:22:05,307
In the end, you could say the only one who
could have given it to her was Motoki-san.

399
00:22:05,808 --> 00:22:07,443
Hang on a minute!

400
00:22:07,543 --> 00:22:10,479
If I tried to force such a thing on Nana-chan,
she would have gone berserk!

401
00:22:10,579 --> 00:22:12,247
You didn't do it by force.

402
00:22:13,215 --> 00:22:17,653
I'm sure the two of you...
agreed to it.

403
00:22:18,887 --> 00:22:23,726
Right, bride Kanon-san?

404
00:22:25,060 --> 00:22:30,499
Kanon-san, you had realized full well
that something was going on between them.

405
00:22:31,967 --> 00:22:33,736
When you were in the kitchen...

406
00:22:34,036 --> 00:22:38,173
...you substituted out the Sonsho seasoning
and replaced it with soba flour.

407
00:22:38,273 --> 00:22:39,308
"Soba Flour"

408
00:22:39,408 --> 00:22:42,778
And then, while gesturing that
you were adding Sonsho to the curry...

409
00:22:43,112 --> 00:22:46,215
...you were actually adding soba
and then you ate that.

410
00:22:50,285 --> 00:22:51,387
Kanon.

411
00:22:51,920 --> 00:22:54,022
Kanon, why?

412
00:22:54,256 --> 00:22:55,891
Was it to fix the blame on me?

413
00:22:55,991 --> 00:22:57,226
Why?

414
00:22:57,626 --> 00:22:59,661
That's the line I should be asking!

415
00:23:00,496 --> 00:23:02,264
Even though I trusted you...

416
00:23:02,798 --> 00:23:06,201
Even though I trusted you,
why did you kiss Nana?

417
00:23:08,070 --> 00:23:10,105
Nana-chan and him kissed?!

418
00:23:10,672 --> 00:23:12,708
I understand even less now.

419
00:23:13,108 --> 00:23:15,344
A person can't die from a kiss, can they?

420
00:23:15,844 --> 00:23:18,046
A person can't die from a kiss, can they?

421
00:23:18,147 --> 00:23:22,484
Well, when a person intends to kill...

422
00:23:23,819 --> 00:23:25,988
...they can kill with a kiss.

423
00:23:27,923 --> 00:23:34,296
Kanon-san kissed Motoki-san immediately after
eating curry that had been laced with soba.

424
00:23:34,530 --> 00:23:38,901
At that time, soba ingredients
were on Motoki-san's lips.

425
00:23:39,001 --> 00:23:43,105
And then Motoki-san passed it on to Nana-san.

426
00:23:43,539 --> 00:23:46,175
But... that fidelity kiss was...

427
00:23:46,408 --> 00:23:48,977
A kiss is an essential part
of a wedding, right?

428
00:23:49,978 --> 00:23:51,713
You planned it on that assumption, didn't you?

429
00:23:51,847 --> 00:23:53,215
Hold on a minute!

430
00:23:53,315 --> 00:23:54,950
There's no way Kanon could do
such a thing, now is there!?

431
00:23:55,050 --> 00:23:56,852
I did put it in!!

432
00:24:00,022 --> 00:24:04,326
If you and Nana weren't having an affair,
then nothing would have happened.

433
00:24:04,927 --> 00:24:09,598
My curry would have tasted a little bad is all.

434
00:24:11,133 --> 00:24:14,002
I even intentionally sent a telegram
giving the two of you a warning.

435
00:24:14,002 --> 00:24:15,070
"If you have an affair, I'll kill you"

436
00:24:15,604 --> 00:24:19,107
Nana wouldn't have died...

437
00:24:19,408 --> 00:24:22,411
But it couldn't be helped, could it?
She paid the price.

438
00:24:22,811 --> 00:24:24,913
When Ken-chan and her kissed.

439
00:24:26,949 --> 00:24:31,453
"Nana-chan... are you really pregnant?"

440
00:24:33,355 --> 00:24:35,390
"That was a lie..."

441
00:24:35,524 --> 00:24:36,959
"Eh!?"

442
00:24:37,192 --> 00:24:41,196
"But I'll say that unless you kiss me."

443
00:24:47,169 --> 00:24:50,906
I... killed Nana-chan?

444
00:24:51,373 --> 00:24:53,475
It was inevitable she would be killed.

445
00:24:53,575 --> 00:24:55,310
That's the kind of woman she was.

446
00:24:55,844 --> 00:24:58,547
A vulgar woman who wanted
what other people had.

447
00:24:58,647 --> 00:25:00,382
That was Nana!

448
00:25:00,916 --> 00:25:02,417
Beautiful...

449
00:25:03,118 --> 00:25:05,988
Getting anything she could think of...

450
00:25:06,154 --> 00:25:08,090
Whatever was best for herself...

451
00:25:08,423 --> 00:25:10,192
Such a woman...

452
00:25:10,926 --> 00:25:12,728
...should be dead.

453
00:25:21,303 --> 00:25:23,805
Shall you go with us to our office?

454
00:25:24,206 --> 00:25:26,441
Motoki-san, you too.

455
00:25:27,376 --> 00:25:28,777
Come, let's go.

456
00:25:33,815 --> 00:25:39,922
Nana-chan was so envious of Kanon-chan
that she couldn't stand it.

457
00:25:42,658 --> 00:25:43,625
Eh?

458
00:25:43,926 --> 00:25:48,764
Only non-serious men like me
approached her due to her looks...

459
00:25:48,964 --> 00:25:51,667
...and there wasn't any man
who truly loved her.

460
00:25:51,867 --> 00:25:54,736
But, a proper man had come
to Kanon-chan...

461
00:25:54,836 --> 00:25:57,139
...one who was thinking of
a future together with her.

462
00:25:58,206 --> 00:25:59,975
Such a thing...

463
00:26:00,542 --> 00:26:04,413
Nana couldn't have envied me.

464
00:26:04,947 --> 00:26:08,483
I think she held a complex about you...

465
00:26:08,817 --> 00:26:13,722
...just as you held a complex about her.

466
00:26:13,822 --> 00:26:15,223
I'm sure of it.

467
00:26:15,324 --> 00:26:18,660
That's why she wanted what you had.

468
00:26:19,661 --> 00:26:23,899
If both of you had been more honest
and quarreled more...

469
00:26:24,766 --> 00:26:28,036
...then you could have been
the truest of friends.

470
00:26:41,116 --> 00:26:42,718
Kanon-san...

471
00:26:53,061 --> 00:26:54,963
I guess I don't get it.

472
00:26:55,897 --> 00:26:58,567
Trying to steal away
your friend's wedding partner...

473
00:26:58,834 --> 00:27:01,937
Trying to kill your friend...

474
00:27:02,838 --> 00:27:06,908
Well, a child like you
still has a lot to learn, huh?

475
00:27:07,342 --> 00:27:11,279
The world of adults is a complicated one.

476
00:27:12,014 --> 00:27:13,281
Still, well...

477
00:27:13,382 --> 00:27:15,651
...you did take your chance
to get a kiss today...

478
00:27:15,751 --> 00:27:16,985
No, I didn't kiss!

479
00:27:17,085 --> 00:27:18,553
Hey!

480
00:27:18,887 --> 00:27:20,756
What was that about a kiss?

481
00:27:20,856 --> 00:27:22,157
Ran!

482
00:27:22,257 --> 00:27:25,260
Ran, you're wrong.
I was only investigating.

483
00:27:25,394 --> 00:27:26,995
That's right. No kissing...

484
00:27:27,763 --> 00:27:29,564
There no arguing about it.

485
00:27:35,303 --> 00:27:38,707
Ah, so that was it, huh?

486
00:27:39,041 --> 00:27:40,275
Then...

487
00:27:40,475 --> 00:27:43,145
Shin'ichi hasn't had his First Kiss yet...

488
00:27:44,446 --> 00:27:46,248
I see, I see.

489
00:27:46,548 --> 00:27:47,616
Huh?

490
00:27:48,817 --> 00:27:49,985
Okay!

491
00:27:50,085 --> 00:27:52,521
I know what characters
to input into the panel...

492
00:27:52,621 --> 00:27:53,989
Not even hesitating, huh?

493
00:27:55,090 --> 00:27:57,392
"Kiss"

494
00:28:01,763 --> 00:28:03,498
Okay, let's go!

495
00:28:03,799 --> 00:28:06,601
Ah! The dress...

496
00:28:06,735 --> 00:28:09,538
It'd probably be better
to have a new one made, wouldn't it?

497
00:28:10,672 --> 00:28:11,707
Eh?

498
00:28:12,607 --> 00:28:14,376
You aren't a bride yet!

499
00:28:14,476 --> 00:28:15,377
Huh?!

500
00:28:15,477 --> 00:28:17,579
C'mon, hurry, let's go!

501
00:28:27,355 --> 00:28:30,792
"Which day last year did you first eat saury?"
(type of fish)

502
00:28:30,892 --> 00:28:33,395
Eh? It's impossible to remember
such a thing, isn't it?!

503
00:28:36,832 --> 00:28:39,267
How do you remember something like that?

504
00:28:40,936 --> 00:28:43,271
"When was the day you last drank tea?"

505
00:28:44,206 --> 00:28:46,108
Tea...

506
00:28:46,975 --> 00:28:48,844
Tea, tea...

507
00:28:51,513 --> 00:28:53,381
Oi, this is bad!

508
00:28:54,516 --> 00:28:56,618
This is the sort of atmosphere
where you get an explosion!

509
00:28:56,718 --> 00:28:58,453
Shin'ichi, hurry and remember!

510
00:28:58,553 --> 00:28:59,688
Wait!

511
00:28:59,788 --> 00:29:02,924
Tea. Tea. Tea...

512
00:29:10,065 --> 00:29:14,736
"Wife vs. Lover
A Woman's Pride Makes Murder!"

513
00:29:22,110 --> 00:29:24,146
"This Drama is Fictional"

